WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.485
Security conditions change over time.

2
00:00:02.485 --> 00:00:16.523
A system that was understood during authorization may later experience new vulnerabilities, architecture changes, user changes, dependency changes, incidents, policy updates, or shifts in mission importance.

3
00:00:16.523 --> 00:00:29.863
RMF emphasizes continuous monitoring so organizations can identify changes, evaluate control effectiveness, address emerging risks, and support informed decision making throughout system operation.

4
00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:45.178
Continuous monitoring may include vulnerability scanning, configuration monitoring, log review, incident reporting, control assessments, access reviews, patch tracking, risk register updates, and review of plans of action.

5
00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:48.411
The goal is not to collect data for its own sake.

6
00:00:48.411 --> 00:00:57.152
Monitoring should help stakeholders understand whether controls remain effective, whether risk has changed, and whether new action is needed.

7
00:00:57.152 --> 00:01:00.734
Monitoring also supports accountability after authorization.

8
00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:11.230
If a system changes materially, if a control stops working, or if a high-risk finding remains open, leaders need current information to decide what to do next.

9
00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:15.860
A mature monitoring program connects technical signals to governance decisions.

10
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:24.451
For example, vulnerability trends, failed control checks, delayed remediation, or repeated incidents can all become risk information.

11
00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:30.427
Continuous monitoring makes RMF an ongoing management practice rather than a static approval package.

12
00:01:30.427 --> 00:01:35.925
It keeps the organization aware of current conditions and helps risk decisions evolve with the system.

13
00:01:35.925 --> 00:01:40.356
For operational teams, monitoring also creates early warning.

14
00:01:40.356 --> 00:01:50.203
Current evidence can reveal control drift, delayed remediation, repeated weaknesses, or system changes that should be reviewed before they become larger issues.
